 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-012\", \"clauses\": {\"read_and_write\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"F11 has the learner set the clock to a time, which is the writing direction; F12 asks the learner to read the clock, so together they cover both directions. F11 is the single family that best produces the task. Its time_str printed values are clock times at hour, half-hour and quarter-hour positions.\"}, \"time\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"F11 presents a clock time as the object of the task. Its printed time_str values are clock times at hour, half-hour and quarter-hour positions only.\"}, \"hour\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"{hour}:00\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 gives a whole-hour time from hour 1 to 12 with minute 0, which is the hour range the competency names. Its domain is a number in a range from 1 to 12 and it is not in the failing set.\"}, \"half_hour\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"The printed time_str values of F11 include half-hour positions, for example 10:30, 11:30 and 9:30, so F11 can produce half-hour problems. F11 is not in the failing set.\"}, \"quarter_hour\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Set the clock to show {time_str}{trailing}\", \"reasoning\": \"The printed time_str values of F11 include quarter-hour positions, for example 11:15, 12:45 and 9:45, so F11 can produce quarter-hour problems. F11 is not in the failing set.\"}, \"analog_clock\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F12\", \"template\": \"What time does the clock show?\", \"reasoning\": \"F12 asks the learner to read a clock face, which is the analog clock representation the clause names. Its template is chosen by interaction_mode and it has no slots, so it introduces no out-of-scope value.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F09\", \"F13\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{hour}:{minute:02d}\", \"{hours}:{minutes:02d}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 fills minute from a number in a range of 0 to 59 (basis: a minute of the hour), not only 0, 15, 30 and 45. Its minute value derives from precision, and the declared variants include one_minute and five_minutes, which the competency text does not name. F09 therefore can print minutes that are neither hour, half hour nor quarter hour, in correct_answer, format_data.mcq_options and format_data.time_str. F13 fills hours from a number in a range of 0 to 23 (basis: an hour of the day). That produces 24-hour times, including hour 0 and hours 13 to 23, which are not the 12-hour analog clock face of grade 1 quarter 4 and are beyond the competency. F13 also fills minutes from 0 to 59 in the same way as F09, and it appears in correct_answer, format_data.mcq_options and format_data.time_str. F08, F11, F12, F01 to F07 and F10 stay within hour, half-hour and quarter-hour clock times, with hours 1 to 12, and do not fail. The clause verdicts are all PRODUCIBLE, so the FAIL rests on Rule 1 alone.\"}",
